cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use M-Anchor App, cite this software and identify the source commit or archived version. The app has no Zenodo DOI yet."
type: software
title: "M-Anchor App V1: A Deterministic Gate for Containing Prompt-Induced Unauthorized Record Updates"
authors:
  - family-names: Ise
    alias: iseyan
    website: "https://github.com/iseyan"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iseyan/M-Anchor-App"
url: "https://github.com/iseyan/M-Anchor-App"
abstract: >-
  M-Anchor App is a local Python application that separates model-generated
  proposals from authoritative case-record updates. A deterministic gate checks
  state references, externally admitted evidence, candidate transitions, and
  authority requests before committing an update. The V1 demonstration includes
  four fixed attack types, two controls, and user-supplied records of three model
  runs. Protection is bounded to the configured case store; the application does
  not prevent all prompt attacks or establish the truth of model output.
keywords:
  - prompt injection
  - prompt attacks
  - deterministic gate
  - record integrity
  - AI agents
  - evidence admission
  - candidate preservation
  - M-Anchor
